# Debug Log: NaN in qwen3_forward_c at layer 7

## Bug
C fused forward function qwen3_forward_c produces all-NaN output for Qwen3-30B 7+ layers. Layers 1-6 work correctly (max_logit ~17), layer 7+ produces NaN.

## Model Architecture
- Qwen3-30B: 48 layers, N=2048, NH=32, n_kv_h=4, HD=128, FF_total=6144
- 128 experts, top_k=8, n_ff_expert=768
- Attention weights: Q4_K (type 12), K: Q4_K, V: Q4_K, O: Q4_K
- Expert gate/up: Q4_K (type 12), Expert down: Q6_K (type 14)
- Output weight: Q8_0 (type 8), shape [151936, 2048]

## The C Function
A single #pragma omp parallel region wraps all 48 layers. Inside:
- RMS norm (omp for reduction)
- QKV projection (omp for per-row quant_matmul_omp calls)
- RoPE (omp for)
- KV cache update (omp single)
- GQA inline attention (omp for over kv_heads)
- Output projection (omp single calls quant_matmul_omp)
- RMS norm again (omp for reduction)  
- MoE via moe_forward_omp (omp single calls moe_forward_omp)

## What's Been Checked
1. Individual quant_matmul_omp calls work from Python ✓
2. L=1..6 work correctly in the C function ✓
3. NaN detection after norm, QKV, GQA all show NO NaN ✓
4. NaN detection AFTER the MoE (ffn_out check with abort()) also shows NO NaN

## Critical Unresolved
The NaN check AFTER `x[i] = res[i] + ffn_out[i]` (after MoE residual) also shows NO NaN with abort().
But the final logits are ALL NaN (151936 elements).
This means NaN appears in the OUTPUT PROJECTION section (after the parallel region ends).
The output projection does:
   1. Final RMS norm on x
   2. quantize_q8_0_c(x, xn_q8, N)  
   3. quant_matmul_omp(w_out, x, logits, 151936, 2048, 8)
The output weight is Q8_0 type 8 with shape [151936, 2048].

